# Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting: "Strange new worlds — Lt. Arex's power and toughness are each equal to the number of
# differently named lands you control" (CR 604.3, 613.4a): a characteristic-defining ability, so it reads the current
# lands through the layers and applies in every zone. "You control" excludes Bot2's lands, a repeated land name counts
# once, and "each ... equal" makes both power and toughness the same number. Trample is on the card.

[Bot1 Deck]
Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Island
Plains
Forest
Mountain
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mountain
Forest
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Island; Plains)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
# Bot1 has Forest, Island, Plains - three differently named lands - so Lt. Arex is 3/3.
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting.Toughness = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Lt. Arex, Ever-Adapting.Keywords = Trample
